  "question": {
    "text": "The transverse displacement $y(x, t)$ of a wave on a string is given by \r\n$y(x, t)=e^{-\\left(a x^{2}+b t^{2}+2 \\sqrt{a b}\\right.}$ xt $)$\r\nThis represents a",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "GgdN3",
      "text": "wave moving in $-x$ direction, speed $\\sqrt{\\frac{b}{a}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sPqnL",
      "text": "standing wave of frequency $\\sqrt{b}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "noqMM",
      "text": "standing wave of frequency $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{b}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cy1Qs",
      "text": "wave moving in $+x$ direction, speed $\\sqrt{\\frac{a}{b}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$y(x, t)=e^{-\\left(a x^{2}+b t^{2}+2 \\sqrt{a b} x t\\right)}=e^{-(\\sqrt{a x}+\\sqrt{b t})^{2}}$\r\nIt is a function of type $y=f(\\omega t+k x)$ $\\therefore y(x, t)$ represents wave travelling along $-x$ direction.\r\n$\\text { Speed of wave }=\\frac{\\omega}{k}=\\frac{\\sqrt{b}}{\\sqrt{a}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{b}{a}}$",
